00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
In this video, I will show you how to make a twist panel as shown in the video.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Today, let's make a twist panel as shown in the video.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
First, let's use the plus point line tool to score.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:24,000
This is a reference for the position of the seam allowance.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Then, we switch to the edit panel tool and use the internal line tool.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
In the position we need to add, add an internal line of 1 to 8 mm.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Note that if you need to cancel the extension of the internal line here, you will create an internal line in parallel.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
This internal line will be our reference line for adding the seam allowance.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Next, we add the internal circle on the end point of the corresponding internal line.

10
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Set the diameter to 10 mm and then click OK.

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Then this circle is the position of the twist panel that we want to fix.

12
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Now let's copy it and paste it out.

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Click on the position that needs to be pasted and click OK.

14
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,000
You can see that there are several points that need to be pasted.

15
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Next, let's separate the points on the internal circle.

16
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:21,000
This is convenient for the next process.

17
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Because we only need a semi-circular fixed panel line here, so we delete the other half.

18
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:34,000
OK, so now we have a semi-circular.

19
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Next, we use the twist tool to add the extension at the center point of the corresponding circle.

20
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Then switch to the select move twist tool.

21
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:51,000
First copy the first twist, then right-click on the appropriate position and paste the twist to the position below.

22
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:57,000
It is the same, right-click on the position that needs to be pasted, you can add multiple extension twists.

23
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Then we need to set the twist layer.

24
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Harden the panels in the middle.

25
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Make them a little closer to the middle.

26
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,000
You can also make the two-layer panels flatter.

27
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Then turn off the simulation.

28
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Next, set the layer of sewing here.

29
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,000
I have two layers here.

30
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,000
You can also make the two-layer panels flatter.

31
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,000
You can also make the two-layer panels flatter.

32
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Then turn off the simulation.

33
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Next, we use the twist tool to add the extension.

34
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,000
The width is set to 30 mm.

35
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Then the height is set to 1 mm.

36
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
We switch to the add point division tool.

37
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,000
First add a point to the edge to make it easier to locate.

38
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Then right-click on the position at the bottom edge.

39
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Switch to the length division.

40
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:07,000
In the middle, separate a section of 8 mm in length.

41
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Set the direction as the center.

42
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Then this section, go with our half-circle position.

43
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Go to the center to make a seam.

44
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:36,000
The two ends of the panel line are fixed to the other side.

45
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Pay attention to the direction of the seam on both ends.

46
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:50,000
The middle can be separated a little bit.

47
